sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 (one task:cancel; ending a group with cleanup is its own action kind), docs/reference/tasks.md "Cancel a stuck task", DECISIONS R2-R4, Nick 2026-11-06: the push step mints its token when it runs, and a task VM never holds a GitHub credential.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 16, 20 (no power read first: each guest step carries a guard on the VM's power, and the delete is safe to repeat).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tasks:cancel
  %% kind: tasks.cancel
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>tvm-88 over ssh
  participant H as Incus host<br/>Node 14 · VM power
  CLI->>GW: tasks:cancel 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit tasks:cancel 42 --yes`
  %%> - syntax: `[group] [--yes] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the task group id; omitting it uses the standard selector
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--yes`, the CLI first asks to cancel group 42 and remove its task VM; the default is No
  %%> Also:
  %%> - `tasks:complete 42` admits the same ending when its pull request merged or closed; the group then ends `completed`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool `tasks-cancel` send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the end<br/>task #5141 · group 42 ending
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has Gateway access, and the Tasks extension is on
  %%> - group 42 is not `completed`, and not `settling` with a pull request (complete it instead)
  %%> - no other ending task holds `task_group:42`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5141 recorded with the full intent: VM 88, Node 14, the workspace, its Route, the teardown steps and the last approved commit
  %%> - a group with no workspace ends `cancelled` at once, with no run (R1)
  GW->>SW: Cancel the group run<br/>native cancel · task #5140
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - cancels the group's root task; Swamp cancels its running Pi turn or check and tears down their SSH sessions
  %%> Busy:
  %%> - the Gateway waits briefly for the terminal event within the budget; a run that does not end returns `operation.target_busy`, and nothing changes
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-cancel
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - VM 88, Node 14, the checkout path and its SSH host key; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5141
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number and a compact input summary; the full execution plan stays in the Gateway
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  opt approved work not on origin
    SW->>VM: Push approved work<br/>git bundle · task-42 · no force
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - exports the approved commit as a Git bundle and pushes it from 209, so you can open a pull request from `task-42`
    %%> - admission names the vault key of the push token; the push step asks the Gateway for the token (`operation:direct:github-token`) right before the push, and the VM never holds it
    %%> - uncommitted changes are never pushed
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the run stops before any removal, so the work stays in the VM
    %%> Guard:
    %%> - runs only while VM 88 runs; guest steps never run on a stopped VM, so no power read runs first
  end
  Note over SW: Withdraw the Route<br/>@swamp/ssh · only this workspace
  %%> When:
  %%> - only when one Route targets this workspace alone; a shared or foreign Route refuses the end
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the Route's Caddy site on its Node before the VM goes
  opt VM still running
    SW->>VM: Run teardown steps<br/>Project teardown · own timeouts
    %%> When:
    %%> - a `guard` on the provider's power state: only while VM 88 runs; a stopped VM skips guest teardown
    %%> How:
    %%> - each command writes its output to a file on the VM; `output_copy` downloads them and `output` keeps a redacted 4 KiB tail of each, so raw output never reaches native history
  end
  SW->>H: Destroy the task VM<br/>delete VM · revoke model key
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes VM 88 and revokes its model key
  %%> Per provider:
  %%> - Incus: `incus delete` on Node 14 over SSH
  %%> - UpCloud overflow: the UpCloud API from 209
  %%> Guard:
  %%> - skipped when the task has no VM, or when the Route is not withdrawn; the check below then reads the VM as not destroyed and the run fails
  SW->>H: Check the VM is gone<br/>provider absence
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the VM only counts as removed when the provider no longer has it
  alt every step passes
    H-->>SW: VM 88 absent
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>group 42 cancelled · VM 88 gone
    %%> Result:
    %%> - group 42 and its open subtasks are `cancelled`; comments, threads and transcripts stay as history
    %%> - the workspace Instance, its Route record, VM 88 and the `tvm-88` Node record are removed
    %%> - task #5141 succeeds
  else a step fails
    H--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or VM still there
    %%> When:
    %%> - the push, Route withdrawal, teardown or deletion fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the records<br/>group asks for help · rerun cancel
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5141 fails; group 42 keeps its status, its workspace and VM 88, and asks for `removal_failure` assistance
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - steps done before the failure stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run `tasks:cancel 42` again after fixing the cause; it is a new task, and done steps find nothing left to do
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5141
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
